            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0239" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3776: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Nanking (Peck) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-31T10:00:00+08:00">January 31, 1932—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 31—12:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. In execution of formulated plan the most important officers of the Chinese
                    Government have temporarily removed their offices from Nanking.</p>
                <p>Four Japanese destroyers have just arrived and anchored. I have telephoned to the
                    Japanese Consul in my capacity of Senior Consul and he has again assured me that
                    the Japanese vessels will not take the initiative in fire action.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
